.TH SINGCTL 1 "2026" "singctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
singctl \- VLESS proxy / VPN client on an embedded sing-box core
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo singctl
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B singctl
runs a VLESS proxy on an embedded sing-box core and toggles a system-wide VPN
(TUN) mode from a terminal UI. It passively coexists with Cisco Secure Client
(observe-only): while a corporate VPN is connecting or active, singctl yields
the routing table to avoid AnyConnect's IP-forwarding integrity check.
.PP
Two sing-box instances are managed: a persistent PROXY (local SOCKS on
127.0.0.1:1080 and HTTP on 127.0.0.1:2080 by default) and an on-demand
TUN forwarder used only in VPN mode.
.PP
The shipping binary is built with the
.B singbox
build tag; the default build links a stub core for the hermetic test suite.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIvless://...\fR
VLESS key (link) to load. May be given more than once to register several
servers; the proxy then picks the fastest reachable one automatically
(latency-tested, priority follows the order given).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without the terminal UI. Requires a key from
.BR \-\-key ,
.B $SINGCTL_KEY
or the saved profile.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-logs
Stream sing-box logs to stdout (headless) or open the logs view on start (TUI).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Verbose sing-box logging (level=info). The default is a quiet
.B warn
level, which keeps errors but drops the per-connection log firehose.
.TP
.B \-\-vpn
Enable VPN (TUN) mode on start.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-proxy
Enable proxy mode on start.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run detached in the background and exit, so the proxy keeps running after the
terminal closes. Re-execs singctl headless with setsid; the key is loaded from
the saved profile. Manage the background process with
.BR \-\-status ", " \-\-attach " and " \-\-stop .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
Local SOCKS port (HTTP proxy listens on port+1; defaults: 1080/2080).
.TP
.BI \-\-clash\-api " host:port"
Address of sing-box's Clash API, used for enriched connection logging (source
process, full destination, outbound chain) and per-server latency. Bound to
loopback with a random secret. Default: 127.0.0.1:9090.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-clash\-api
Disable the Clash API (no connection logging or latency metrics).
.TP
.BI \-\-clash\-secret " s"
Clash API secret. Default: a random token generated per run.
.TP
.BI \-\-urltest\-url " url"
Probe URL used to latency-test servers for failover. Default: gstatic
generate_204.
.TP
.BI \-\-urltest\-interval " d"
How often servers are re-probed (e.g. 3m). Default: 3m.
.TP
.BI \-\-urltest\-tolerance " ms"
Latency hysteresis before switching the active server. Default: 50.
.TP
.BI \-\-route\-pid " pid"
Route an already-running process's traffic through the proxy. Linux only
(cgroup v2 + nftables); repeatable. Requires VPN mode (the TUN must be up).
.TP
.B \-\-launch " \-\- cmd args..."
Run a command with its traffic routed through the proxy. On Linux this uses real
interception; on other platforms it injects proxy environment variables
(HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY/ALL_PROXY) into the child, which only covers env-aware
applications.
.TP
.BI \-\-restart\-pid " pid"
Recover a running process's command line, terminate it, and relaunch it routed
through the proxy. Best-effort (argv via ps); the only way to proxy an
already-running process on macOS. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-attach
Attach to an already-running singctl instance (started, e.g., with
.B \-\-headless
in another tab) and live-tail its log. Ctrl+C detaches without stopping it.
Runs without root.
.PP
Note: simply launching
.B singctl
again while an instance is already running does NOT start a second proxy (which
would fail to bind the port) — the new TUI automatically ATTACHES to the running
instance and can change its mode/settings/keys in real time over the control
socket. A second
.B \-\-headless
launch applies the requested mode (\-\-proxy/\-\-vpn) to the running instance and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Tell the running instance to shut down. Runs without root.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the running instance's status (PID, mode, start time). Runs without root.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt for destructive actions
.RB ( \-\-stop ", " \-\-restart\-pid ).
Useful for scripts.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " path"
Load environment variables from this file (default: ./.env if present).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Do not persist the key to ~/.config/singctl.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Print this man page (roff) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-license " token|path"
Install a license (a token string or a path to a file containing one) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-license\-status
Print the current license status and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-email " address"
Contact email to register with \-\-license for device activation (resent on re-activation and daily rechecks).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SINGCTL_KEY
VLESS key, used when
.B \-\-key
is not given. May contain several newline-separated links.
.TP
.B SINGCTL_KEYS
Several newline/semicolon-separated VLESS keys for failover.
.TP
.B SINGCTL_PORT
SOCKS port, used when
.B \-\-port
is not given.
.TP
.B SINGCTL_CLASH_API
Clash API address, used when
.B \-\-clash\-api
is left at its default.
.TP
.B SINGCTL_CLASH_SECRET
Clash API secret, used when
.B \-\-clash\-secret
is unset.
.PP
These variables can also be placed in a .env file in the working directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/singctl/profile.txt
Saved VLESS key(s).
.TP
.B ~/.config/singctl/singbox.log
sing-box log output (TUI mode).
.SH NOTES
singctl must run as root: creating the TUN device and managing routes requires
privileges. Re-run with
.BR sudo .
.PP
Applications started or restarted through the proxy
.RB ( \-\-launch ", " \-\-restart\-pid ,
or the in-UI picker) are dropped back to the invoking user (resolved via
.BR SUDO_USER )
rather than inheriting root, so GUI apps that refuse to run as root in a user's
session (e.g. Zen) start correctly.
.SH SEE ALSO
sing-box(1)
